; Print a 5-digit decimal number
;
; Prints HL as exactly five decimal digits (leading zeros are printed) in the
; character cells starting at DE, using #R$6B48 and #R$6B4F. Used for the
; score and the best score on the status line. Nothing is drawn while bit 0 of
; the flag at #R$6B0B is clear (demo mode).
; Hardware: writes the screen bitmap and attributes (via #R$6C0F and
; #R$6B4F).
;
; DE Screen address of the first digit (first pixel row of the cell)
; HL Number to print (0-65535)
; O:DE Screen address of the cell after the last digit
; O:HL Units digit (0-9)
; O:A ASCII "0" when printing is enabled
; O:BC 10
@label=PrintNumber
c$6B21 EX DE,HL      ;
 $6B22 CALL $6C0F    ;
 $6B25 EX DE,HL      ;
@isub=LD A,CHAR_0
 $6B26 LD A,$30      ;
 $6B28 AND A         ;
@isub=LD BC,10000
 $6B29 LD BC,$2710   ;
 $6B2C CALL $6B48    ;
@isub=LD BC,1000
 $6B2F LD BC,$03E8   ;
 $6B32 CALL $6B48    ;
@isub=LD BC,100
 $6B35 LD BC,$0064   ;
 $6B38 CALL $6B48    ;
@isub=LD BC,10
 $6B3B LD BC,$000A   ;
 $6B3E CALL $6B48    ;
; The remainder is the units digit
 $6B41 LD A,L        ;
@isub=ADD A,CHAR_0
 $6B42 ADD A,$30     ;
 $6B44 CALL $6B4F    ;
 $6B47 RET           ;
